{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t---\n2\tname: turnbridge-mvp-decisions\n3\tdescription: Turnbridge intent decisions (2026-07-19 MVP, 2026-07-21 end-state) and implementation state\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e\n8\t  modified: 2026-08-04T02:50:34.271Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tDecisions made by the user on 2026-07-19 that override the original design docs:\n12\t\n13\t- Turnbridge is the **resume layer only**; conversation-ledger owns capture\n14\t  (its `cledger install` hooks + adapters already existed and are reused).\n15\t- Cross-CLI rehydration **defaults to native session fabrication** (writing\n16\t  target-native session files so the CLI's own resume loads them);\n17\t  `--bootstrap` (transcript-file rehydration) is the explicit fallback.\n18\t- MVP audience: the user hopping CLIs **and** sharing chats with collaborators\n19\t  who use different CLIs — own chats by default, `--all` for others', identity\n20\t  via git `user.email` stamped as `actor.id` (upstream cledger change).\n21\t- Command surface: standalone `turnbridge resume [claude|codex]` is default;\n22\t  the PATH shim (`turnbridge shim install`) is opt-in, may become default\n23\t  later if it proves stable over a few weeks.\n24\t- Picker UX the user described: pick conversation → asked which CLI → offered\n25\t  to save that choice as default.\n26\t\n27\tImplementation state: MVP works end-to-end; fabrication verified against real\n28\tbinaries (claude 2.1.215, codex-cli 0.144.6) via planted-secret resume tests.\n29\tVersion-pinned format specs live in turnbridge `docs/specs/`. Upstream\n30\tconversation-ledger gained `package.json` exports + `gitUserIdentity` actor\n31\tstamping (note: full transcript rescans can duplicate pre-identity events\n32\tsince `actor.id` is part of the event-id hash).\n33\t\n34\tEnd-state decisions from 2026-07-21 (drive TODO priority):\n35\t- **Public npm release** is the goal — the `file:../conversation-ledger` dep\n36\t  must become a published semver dep before turnbridge can publish.\n37\t- **Embrace cledger 0.8.0 auto-re-anchor** (readEvents now may write re_anchor\n38\t  events + print stderr as a side effect): keep it on for lineage-survives-\n39\t  rebase; turnbridge just keeps the stderr noise out of its picker UI.\n40\t- **Verify interactive resume paths now** — all fabrication verification was\n41\t  headless (`-p` / `codex exec`); interactive resume for both CLIs was never\n42\t  content-confirmed.\n43\t- **Deepen Claude Code ⇄ Codex** rather than adding a third CLI target\n44\t  (though the user expects both deepening and broadening before release).\n45\t  *Superseded 2026-08-03:* opencode is now a full third member in both\n46\t  directions — target adapter in turnbridge (PR #3), capture in cledger 0.18.0.\n47\t  See [[local-model-oneshot-evaluation]] for how that PR was produced and\n48\t  reviewed.\n49\t- npm publish of both packages deliberately deferred for a few days of\n50\t  dogfooding; turnbridge's `prepublishOnly` refuses while the ledger dep is\n51\t  `file:`. Both npm names were unclaimed as of 2026-07-21.\n52\t- Drift-agent stage 2 (CI agent drafts revalidation PRs) deferred — the\n53\t  commented-out job lives in `.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml`.\n54\t- As of 2026-07-21: interactive resume verified on both CLIs via\n55\t  `npm run smoke:interactive` (expect-based pty; macOS `script` can't run\n56\t  ptyless) + `scripts/probe-codex-content.mjs`; codex 0.145 validated\n57\t  (prefix list); 61 tests; ledger reads sequenced + stderr-buffered.\n58\t\n59\tTwo non-obvious findings from the 2026-07-19 follow-up session:\n60\t- **Codex TUI scrollback renders from `event_msg` records, not `response_item`.**\n61\t  The model still SEES history from response_items (user confirmed resumed\n62\t  Codex knew the prior context), but the screen looks e