{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01S4AXmAr1rqLizapBR3FNZE","input":{"file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/memory/turnbridge-mvp-decisions.md","new_string":"  *Open bug found 2026-08-05, root-caused 2026-08-06 (opencode 1.18.5):* a\n  **fabricated opencode session cannot be continued**, in the TUI *and* the CLI\n  (human-confirmed in the TUI: the prompt is persisted as a `user` message and\n  no assistant reply is ever generated). Cause, from `--print-logs`:\n  `ProviderModelNotFoundError: Model not found: turnbridge/<model>`. The adapter\n  writes `providerID: \"turnbridge\"` (src/targets/opencode.ts 321/327/388/408),\n  and opencode resolves the agent loop's model from the session's stored\n  provider — **not** from `-m` or the TUI model picker, which is why neither\n  overrides it. Logs show `loop step=0` → `exiting loop`, no `stream` line,\n  where native sessions log `process` → `stream` → `llm runtime selected`.\n  No network request is made, so the provider is never implicated.\n  The spec's §6 claim that the `Model turnbridge/<model> is not valid` toast is\n  cosmetic (\"composer falls back ... renders in full either way\") is **wrong**:\n  the composer falls back, the agent loop does not.\n  Patching only those 4 `providerID` values to `\"opencode\"` makes the model\n  respond **and correctly recall a marker planted in the bridged history** — so\n  fabrication is sound and the model does read bridged context. Real fix must\n  keep the provider resolvable while preserving source-model provenance\n  honestly (the contract forbids substituting a recognized-but-false id).\n  Unconfirmed side observation: after the fix the run answered then regenerated\n  ~237 times until killed — possibly a weak free model, possibly the missing\n  `step-start`/`step-finish` parts on fabricated assistant messages.","old_string":"  *Open bug found 2026-08-05 (opencode 1.18.5):* a **fabricated opencode\n  session cannot be continued** — `opencode run -s <id>` appends the user\n  message and exits **0 with empty output**, no assistant reply, no events even\n  under `--format json`. A native session in the same dir/project/model recalls\n  its marker fine (controlled twice, bracketing the failures), and the failure\n  reproduces across three models, so it is structural, not provider flake.\n  Filed under the *global* project it fails loudly instead\n  (`UnknownError / Unexpected server error`). Two candidate causes, unconfirmed:\n  fabricated assistant messages carry only a `text` part (native ones have\n  `step-start`…`step-finish`), and the import notice makes two consecutive\n  `user` messages open the session. TUI *rendering* was human-verified earlier —\n  only continuation is broken.","replace_all":false},"name":"Edit","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","seq":538},"id":"ev1-9de8185caab7c1b3b123703dd4fa08ed3c62a3f4de3fa307de268db89b59a568","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T04:41:34.801Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.223","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01S4AXmAr1rqLizapBR3FNZE","input":{"file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/memory/turnbridge-mvp-decisions.md","new_string":"  *Open bug found 2026-08-05, root-caused 2026-08-06 (opencode 1.18.5):* a\n  **fabricated op